ref 020 "Multilateration Target Reports Expansion"
edition 1.5
date 2025-07-02

compound 1
    PA "Position Accuracy"
        definition
            Standard Deviation of Position
        compound 1
            DOP "DOP of Position"
                group
                    X "DOP Along X Axis"
                        element 16
                            unsigned quantity 1/2^2 ""
                    Y "DOP Along Y Axis"
                        element 16
                            unsigned quantity 1/2^2 ""
                    XY "DOP Covariance Component"
                        element 16
                            signed quantity 1/2^2 ""
                remark
                    Notes:

                    1. DOP Covariance Component (DOP-xy) = sign {HDOPxy} * sqrt {abs (HDOPxy)}
                    2. "Maximum value" means Maximum value or above.
                    3. From Edition 1.4 of this specification Data Item "High Precision DOP" has een
                       defined. To prevent incompatibilities in receiving systems, the "High Precision
                       DOP" does not replace this "DOP of Position" Data Item but provide additional
                       information. Decoders using this "DOP of Position" Data Item shall continue to
                       provide this Data Item.
            SDC "Standard Deviation of Position (Cartesian)"
                group
                    X "Standard Deviation of X-Component"
                        element 16
                            unsigned quantity 1/2^2 "m"
                    Y "Standard Deviation of Y-Component"
                        element 16
                            unsigned quantity 1/2^2 "m"
                    COV "XY Covariance Component"
                        element 16
                            signed quantity 1/2^2 "m"
                remark
                    Notes:

                    1. XY covariance component = sign {Cov(X,Y)} * sqrt {abs [Cov (X,Y)]}
                    2. "Maximum value" means Maximum value or above.
            SDH "Standard Deviation of Geometric Height (WGS-84)"
                definition
                    Standard deviation of Geometric Height of the target expressed in WGS-84.
                element 16
                    unsigned quantity 1 "ft"
                remark
                    Maximum value means maximum value or above.
            SDW "Standard Deviation of Position (WGS-84)"
                group
                    LAT "Standard Deviation of Latitude Component"
                        element 16
                            unsigned quantity 180/2^25 "°"
                    LON "Standard Deviation of Longitude Component"
                        element 16
                            unsigned quantity 180/2^25 "°"
                    COV "Lat/Long Covariance Component"
                        element 16
                            signed quantity 180/2^25 "°"
                remark
                    Notes:

                    1. WGS-84 covariance component = sign {Cov(Lat,Long)} * sqrt {abs [Cov (Lat,Long)]}
                    2. "Maximum value" means Maximum value or above.
    GVV "Ground Velocity Vector"
        definition
            Ground Speed and Track Angle elements of Ground Velocity Vector.
        group
            RE "Range Exceeded Indicator"
                element 1
                    table
                        0: Value in defined range
                        1: Value exceeds defined range
            GS "Ground Speed"
                element 15
                    unsigned quantity 1/2^14 "NM/s" >= 0 < 2
            TA "Track Angle"
                element 16
                    unsigned quantity 360/2^16 "°"
        remark
            Notes:

            1. The RE-Bit, if set, indicates that the value to be transmitted is beyond the range
               defined for this specific data item and the applied technology. In this case the
               Ground Speed contains the maximum value defined and the RE-bit indicates
               that the actual value is greater than the value contained in the field.
            2. The True North is the geographical north at the position of the aircraft.
            3. This Data Item should be populated by the Ground Velocity Vector as
               calculated by the Multilateration System.
    GVA "Ground Velocity Accuracy"
        definition
            Accuracy of the Ground Speed and Track Angle elements of Ground Velocity Vector.
        group
            GSSD "Standard Deviation of the Ground Speed"
                element 8
                    unsigned quantity 1/2^14 "NM/s" >= 0 < 1/2^6
            TASD "Standard Deviation of the Track Angle"
                element 8
                    unsigned quantity 360/2^12 "°" >= 0 < 45/2
        remark
            Maximum value indicates maximum value or above.
    TRT "Time of ASTERIX Report Transmission"
        definition
            Time of the transmission of the ASTERIX category 020 report in
            the form of elapsed time since last midnight, expressed as UTC.
        element 24
            unsigned quantity 1/2^7 "s"
        remark
            NOTE: The time of ASTERIX report transmission value is reset to zero
            at every midnight. The Time of Report Transmission is the time
            used as a reference for the different data-ages provided in DA.
    DA "Data Ages"
        definition
            Age of specific data-items or subfields at the Time of Report
            Transmission provided in TRT.
        compound
            SPI "Special Position Identification Age"
                definition
                    Age of the Special Position Information (SPI) information
                    transmitted in data item I020/020 SPI field.
                element 8
                    unsigned quantity 1/10 "s"
            TI "Target Identification Age"
                definition
                    Age of the Target Identification information transmitted
                    in data item I020/245.
                element 8
                    unsigned quantity 1/10 "s"
            MBD "BDS Register Data Age"
                definition
                    Age for the BDS Register Data data extracted from aircraft
                    transponder as transmitted in Data item I020/250.
                repetitive 1
                    group
                        BDS1 "Comm B Data Buffer Store 1 Address"
                            element 4
                                raw
                        BDS2 "Comm B Data Buffer Store 2 Address"
                            element 4
                                raw
                        MBA "Age of the Information in the BDS Report"
                            element 8
                                unsigned quantity 1/10 "s"
            M3A "Mode-3/A Code Age"
                definition
                    Age of the information transmitted in data item I020/070.
                element 8
                    unsigned quantity 1/10 "s"
            FL "Flight Level Age"
                definition
                    Age of the information transmitted in data item I020/090.
                element 8
                    unsigned quantity 1/10 "s"
            FS "Flight Status Age"
                definition
                    Age of the Flight Status information transmitted in data
                    item I020/230 STAT subfield.
                element 8
                    unsigned quantity 1/10 "s"
            GH "Geometric / Measured Height Age"
                definition
                    Age of the information transmitted in data item I020/105
                    or in data item I020/110.
                element 8
                    unsigned quantity 1/10 "s"
            TA "Target Address Age"
                definition
                    Age of the Target Address information transmitted in data
                    item I020/220.
                element 8
                    unsigned quantity 1/10 "s"
            MC "Mode C Code Age"
                definition
                    Age of the information transmitted in data item I020/100.
                element 8
                    unsigned quantity 1/10 "s"
            MSS "Mode-S Specific Service Capability Age"
                definition
                    Age of the Mode-S Specific Service Capability information
                    transmitted in data item I020/230 MSSC subfield.
                element 8
                    unsigned quantity 1/10 "s"
            ARC "Altitude Reporting Capability Age"
                definition
                    Age of the Altitude reporting capability information
                    transmitted in item I020/230 ARC subfield.
                element 8
                    unsigned quantity 1/10 "s"
            AIC "Aircraft Identification Capability Age"
                definition
                    Age of the Aircraft Identification Capability information
                    transmitted in data item I020/230 AIC subfield.
                element 8
                    unsigned quantity 1/10 "s"
            M2 "Mode-2 Code Age"
                definition
                    Age of the information transmitted in data item I020/050.
                element 8
                    unsigned quantity 1/10 "s"
            M1 "Mode-1 Code Age"
                definition
                    Age of information transmitted in data item I020/055.
                element 8
                    unsigned quantity 1/10 "s"
            ARA "ACAS Resolution Advisory Age"
                definition
                    Age of the ACAS Advisory Report transmitted in data item
                    I020/260.
                element 8
                    unsigned quantity 1/10 "s"
            VI "Vehicle Fleet Identification Age"
                definition
                    Age of the information transmitted in data item I020/300.
                element 8
                    unsigned quantity 1/10 "s"
            MSG "Pre-programmed Message Age"
                definition
                    Age of the information transmitted in data item I020/310.
                element 8
                    unsigned quantity 1/10 "s"
        remark
            Notes:

            1. In all subfields, the age is the time delay since the latest update received from
               the target.
            2. The ages are provided in reference to the time of the Target Report
               Transmission (TRT) provided in the message.
            3. In all the subfields, the maximum value indicates "maximum value or above".
            4. If the data-item is not transmitted in the target report the corresponding age is
               not transmitted.
            5. The Target Address is considered as received if either it has been received in
               clear in a message or if it has been used to decode a message associated to
               the target.
    HPDOP "High Precision Dilution of Position"
        definition
            Dilution of Precision of the reported Multilateration Position in High Precision.
        group
            X "HPDOP Along X Axis"
                element 16
                    unsigned quantity 1/2^8 "" >= 0 < 256
            Y "HPDOP Along Y Axis"
                element 16
                    unsigned quantity 1/2^8 "" >= 0 < 256
            XY "HPDOP Pearson Correlation Coefficient"
                element 16
                    signed quantity 1/2^15 "" >= -1 < 1
        remark
            Notes:

            1. DOP "Pearson Correlation Coefficient" ρ(X,Y) = DOPxy / (DOPx *
               DOPy) where DOPxy is the DOP Covariance Component.
            2. "Maximum value" means Maximum value or above.
            3. To prevent incompatibilities with existing decoders, this Data
               Item does not replace the "DOP of Position" in Data Item PA,
               Position Accuracy, Subfield #1. Encoders providing "DOP of
               Position" in Data Item PA, Position Accuracy, Subfield #1
               shall continue to do so.
    STRD "Supplementary Target Report Descriptor"
        definition
            Target report descriptor supplementary to I020/020.
        extended
            ADSBCAP "ADS-B Capability Reported by the Target"
                element 4
                    table
                        0: ADS-B Version 0
                        1: ADS-B Version 1
                        2: ADS-B Version 2
                        3: ADS-B Version 3
                        4: Reserved for future use
                        5: Reserved for future use
                        6: Reserved for future use
                        7: Reserved for future use
                        8: Reserved for future use
                        9: Reserved for future use
                        10: Reserved for future use
                        11: Reserved for future use
                        12: Reserved for future use
                        13: Reserved for future use
                        14: No ADS-B
                        15: Information not available
            EHSCAP40 "EHS Capability of the Target for BDS 4,0"
                group
                    EP "Element Populated Bit"
                        element 1
                            table
                                0: Element not populated
                                1: Element populated
                    VAL "EHS Capability for BDS 4,0"
                        element 1
                            table
                                0: Target cannot provide BDS 4,0
                                1: Target can provide BDS 4,0
            EHSCAP50 "EHS Capability of the Target for BDS 5,0"
                group
                    EP "Element Populated Bit"
                        element 1
                            table
                                0: Element not populated
                                1: Element populated
                    VAL "EHS Capability for BDS 5,0"
                        element 1
                            table
                                0: Target cannot provide BDS 5,0
                                1: Target can provide BDS 5,0
            EHSCAP60 "EHS Capability of the Target for BDS 6,0"
                group
                    EP "Element Populated Bit"
                        element 1
                            table
                                0: Element not populated
                                1: Element populated
                    VAL "EHS Capability for BDS 6,0"
                        element 1
                            table
                                0: Target cannot provide BDS 6,0
                                1: Target can provide BDS 6,0
            ATRPS "Active Transponder Side Indicator"
                element 2
                    table
                        0: Information not available
                        1: Transponder #1 (left side or single)
                        2: Transponder #2 (right side)
                        3: Transponder #3 (auxiliary or backup)
            POSMT "Type of Message Used to Calculate the WAM Position"
                definition
                    Type of message used to calculate the WAM position in
                    I020/041 or I020/042
                element 2
                    table
                        0: Information not available
                        1: Mode S message received passively (w/o interrogation)
                        2: Mode S message received in response to an active interrogation
                        3: ADS-B message
            GBSSRC "Source of the Information in I020/020/GBS"
                element 2
                    table
                        0: Information not available
                        1: Mode S message received passively (w/o interrogation)
                        2: Mode S message received in response to an active interrogation
                        3: ADS-B message
            SPISRC "Source of the Information in I020/020/SPI"
                element 2
                    table
                        0: Information not available
                        1: Mode S message received passively (w/o interrogation)
                        2: Mode S message received in response to an active interrogation
                        3: ADS-B message
            ATRPSSRC "Source of the Information in I020/020/ATRPS"
                element 2
                    table
                        0: Information not available
                        1: Mode S message received passively (w/o interrogation)
                        2: Mode S message received in response to an active interrogation
                        3: ADS-B message
            M3ASRC "Source of the Information in I020/070"
                element 2
                    table
                        0: Information not available
                        1: Mode S message received passively (w/o interrogation)
                        2: Mode S message received in response to an active interrogation
                        3: ADS-B message
            FLSRC "Source of the Information in I020/090"
                element 2
                    table
                        0: Information not available
                        1: Mode S message received passively (w/o interrogation)
                        2: Mode S message received in response to an active interrogation
                        3: ADS-B message
            COMSRC "Source of the Position Information in I020/230/COM"
                element 2
                    table
                        0: Information not available
                        1: Mode S message received passively (w/o interrogation)
                        2: Mode S message received in response to an active interrogation
                        3: ADS-B message
            ARCSRC "Source of the Position Information in I020/230/ARC"
                element 2
                    table
                        0: Information not available
                        1: Mode S message received passively (w/o interrogation)
                        2: Mode S message received in response to an active interrogation
                        3: ADS-B message
            ACIDSRC "Source of the Information in I020/245"
                element 2
                    table
                        0: Information not available
                        1: Mode S message received passively (w/o interrogation)
                        2: Mode S message received in response to an active interrogation
                        3: ADS-B message
            ARASRC "Source of the Information in I020/260"
                element 2
                    table
                        0: Information not available
                        1: Mode S message received passively (w/o interrogation)
                        2: Mode S message received in response to an active interrogation
                        3: ADS-B message
            spare 7
            -
        remark
            Note:

            ADSBCAP (bits-40/37) indicates if the target is ADS-B capable and, if yes,
            which version of the ADS-B system is installed.

            ADSBCAP =0 indicates that the target is ADS-B version 0 capable as
            defined in EUROCAE ED-102/RTCA DO-260.

            ADSBCAP =1 indicates that the target is ADS-B version 1 capable as
            defined in RTCA DO-260A for 1090 ES and DO-282 or DO-282A for UAT.

            ADSBCAP =2 indicates that the target is ADS-B version 2 capable as
            defined in EUROCAE ED-102A/RTCA DO-260B for 1090 ES and DO-282B
            for UAT.

            ADSBCAP =3 indicates that the target is ADS-B version 3 capable as
            defined in EUROCAE ED-102B/RTCA DO-260C for 1090 ES and DO-282C
            for UAT.
    GEN20 "Generic Category 020 Data"
        definition
            Placeholder for the addition of information to Category 020 even if
            all bits of the Item Indicator are allocated.
        compound
            -
        remark
            Notes:

            1. For this version of the specification no Sub-Items have been defined for this
               Item.
            2. The definition of additional subitems to I020/REF/GEN20 is the responsibility
               of the AMG and shall be agreed upon prior to implementation.
